      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1004,
          "quote": "- every local disambiguation binds one exact term, target context, complete\n  material candidate set, selected concept, authority, basis, and scope, and\n  `resolves_to` is a member of `disambiguates` and its referenced resolution\n  carrier is congruent with those bindings;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSTDO%20Product%20Definition%20Overlay%20And%20Layout%20Independence%2FRecursive%20Discovery%20And%20Explicit%20Composition",
          "start_line": 1001
        }
      ],
      "key": "discovered_set_conformance",
      "statement": "Every definition validates against its selected released schema; every required URI/fragment resolves within declared workspace/resolver boundaries; definition IDs are globally unique and tenant IDs unique within their overlay. Every governed scope has a resolvable applicable frame basis, with overlaps reconciled by cited authority. Every local disambiguation binds an exact term, target context, complete material candidate set, selected member, authority, basis and scope with congruent resolution carrier. Every material cross-context seam uses explicit import/disambiguation/translation/equivalence, never name matching. Every composition target has the expected ID and every relation/non-empty contract set resolves. No two carriers claim the same Product, tenant, ticket-state or constitutional-relation authority. Draft 2020-12 validation establishes shape only; URI formats are annotations unless asserted. Conformance explicitly checks RFC 3986 URI/reference syntax using assertion-capable validation, then separately resolution, fragments, selected-release identity, cross-file uniqueness, constitutional sufficiency, semantic/cross-context completeness and authority congruence.",
      "uncertainty": "The selected released schemas and resolver configuration are not supplied."
    },
    {
