      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1034,
          "quote": "| `User` | Product role, human person, identity principal, account, actor, operator, or data subject | unresolved until downstream authority defines or explicitly relates the applicable meanings |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSTDO%20Product%20Definition%20Overlay%20And%20Layout%20Independence%2FSemantic-Resolution%20Conformance%20Cases",
          "start_line": 1034
        }
      ],
      "key": "semantic_collision_and_negative_cases",
      "statement": "At minimum, Frame evaluation context and consumer runtime carrier remain distinct without nominal enrollment; Owner specialist family gains no semantic/decision owner authority; immutable Product and mutable Product Definition remain distinct and occurrence context selects; build Tenant supplies no default for hosted/customer/account/runtime/data tenancy; User remains unresolved among Product role, human, principal, account, actor, operator and data subject until downstream authority defines or explicitly relates applicable meanings. Negative cases cover zero candidates, multiple candidates after disambiguation, selection outside the candidate set, context-free glossary fallback, incomplete coordinates, authority/basis mismatch, undeclared loss and invalidated relations. Correct downstream behavior from guessed meaning does not pass semantic conformance.",
