      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1071,
          "quote": "A projected prohibition cannot lose its condition or lawful\nalternative even when every source digest is correct. A summary, bootstrap or\nindex cannot require a stricter or weaker relation by compression. Its\nreferences must be resolvable within the declared actor's access; otherwise the\nrequired meaning is supplied directly.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FOne%20Constitutional%20Surface%20And%20Version%20Boundary%20%28%60STDO-SURFACE-001%60%29",
          "start_line": 1067
        }
      ],
      "key": "constitutional_surface_fidelity",
      "statement": "Views cannot alter a claim's meaning or authority under its selected constitution. Release authority admits one complete cut; derived/installed/mutable surfaces cannot be partial constitutions or reinterpret owners. Derived guidance preserves applicability, obligations, permissions, exclusions, decision owners and invalidators, including conditioned prohibitions and lawful alternatives; compression may neither strengthen nor weaken relations. References must be accessible to the declared actor or their required meaning supplied directly. STDO owns normative algebra, authority, abstract state/transition/admissibility/order/evidence laws; consumers own concrete types, schemas, files, tools, runtime/orchestration, tests and executable conformance. Expanding STDO Product scope through an amendment into a tool, engine, runtime, assurance system or consumer realization requires separate explicit human authorization. A recording agent cannot widen a ruling's subject, implication, authority or change class. Only released versions are publication authority; mutable source may author a future cut but cannot silently govern consumers.",
      "uncertainty": "F2/F3/F6 and the faithful-projection contract are referenced but not supplied in full."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["constitutional_chain"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [
        "A concrete path is a requirement-level choice when the path itself is constitutional.",
        "Tenant-local realization becomes governing truth only when ratified in specification."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1140,
          "quote": "Discarding that context does not rewind A. A new observation can\ninvalidate a belief or dependent result; it cannot silently change Z or create\npermission. Revising Z follows the owning re-entry relation below.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FConstitutional%20Chain",
          "start_line": 1138
        }
      ],
      "key": "constitutional_chain_preservation",
      "statement": "Downstream success needs adequate upstream meaning and traceable authority. Goals/Product owners choose outcomes; Design chooses any constraint-permitted realization, not a uniquely derived implementation. Every chain link is load-bearing: missing repricing, unowned requirements, ungrounded design or realization without design creates accidental law. Projections are checked against source/current state, add no truth surface and require no universal event replay. Intake selects repricing class/owner; a constitutional gap changes that layer and affected downstream span without inherently requiring new Goals/Intent; unresolved causes may need observation. The workspace persists: current material state and valid authority define A, admitted acceptance constraints define Z, and sufficient context supports the next bounded transition. Context loss does not rewind A; observations can invalidate beliefs/results but cannot change Z or create permission. Temporary Goals focus enters deeper law only through intentional repricing. Requirements encompass all constitutional truth; Design selects concrete placement/mechanism unless constitutionally fixed. Physical layout does not alter shared what versus one-or-more how.build_tenants; tenant-local realization remains derivative until ratified.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["sprint"],
      "conditions": [
        "A sprint is used under existing Goals, Intent, Product Definition, Requirements and Design authority."
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1196,
          "quote": "Deferred compliance inside a sprint is escrow, not acceptance. It cannot satisfy\nmethod, release, or product closure until it is paid down, explicitly accepted\nunder the governing method, or repriced into the appropriate upstream surface.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSprint%20Execution%20Boundary",
          "start_line": 1194
        }
      ],
      "key": "sprint_scope_escrow_and_close",
      "statement": "A sprint cannot create, supersede, weaken or override constitutional authority. At minimum it declares served goal/wave, upstream authorities, admitted scope, excluded Product/requirement/design/runtime/data-contract/governance boundaries, expected change classes, any deferrable local proof/compliance debt, closure trigger/law and debt paydown/repricing route. Deferral is lawful only while local, visible, bounded and repayable; escrow cannot satisfy method/release/Product closure until paid, explicitly accepted under governing method or repriced upstream. Close may be recommended, not automatically required, on expired timebox, reached scope, review becoming cheaper than iteration, unsafe review uncertainty or gaps outgrowing the sprint. Close compares work/evidence with authority, classifies every gap, accepts compliant work, opens local paydown and escalates drift lawfully; it is not automatic approval. Discovered truth changes are not authorized by the manifest and must be split, escalated, repriced or explicit paydown. Ticket mechanics and domain-specific escrow suitability remain externally owned.",
      "uncertainty": "TICKET_METHOD and UX_METHOD mechanics are not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["ambiguity_governance"],
      "conditions": [
        "A material unresolved interpretation or major boundary."
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "Risk policy may permit bounded ambiguity handling but cannot override hard stops."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1270,
          "quote": "Ambiguity detection is mandatory. Blocking is policy.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FAmbiguity%20Governance%20Rule",
          "start_line": 1270
        }
      ],
      "key": "ambiguity_detection_and_policy",
      "statement": "Unsupported meaning cannot establish a result or permission. Graph/runtime F_D/F_P/F_H shorthands remain in graph-native ODD unless explicitly imported/translated. The chain progressively narrows priority, direction/scope, Product shape/terms, obligation, executable class, structure and local detail, not uniformly. Major ambiguity must always be surfaced and governed, never hidden in informal judgment, precedent or silent model choice. At each major boundary detect/record remaining or introduced major ambiguity, affected invariant/asset/decision boundary, any decision to proceed, and resolved/carried/escalated/blocked handling. Declared Product risk policy determines allowable probabilistic processing and required human adjudication thresholds; convenience does not. Lower risk appetite escalates more, higher permits more bounded processing; both record ambiguity and decision. The goal is sufficient progressive constraint, not eliminating all ambiguity before work.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["ambiguity_governance"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1324,
          "quote": "Admissibility and fulfillment of the interrupted task remain separate\npredicates: refusal alone does not establish that the intended outcome failed.\nAn unusable governing\nbasis or an evaluation outside capability retains its own diagnosis. The stop\nlabel proves neither non-performance nor absence of effects; an undeclared or\nuncertain effect needs actual observation before dependent action.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FAmbiguity%20Governance%20Rule",
          "start_line": 1319
        }
